<% content_for :title, "InternalQ · AI knowledge assistant for Slack teams" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "InternalQ lets your team ask questions about internal documents directly in Slack. Upload handbooks, policies and SOPs — get instant AI-powered answers cited from your own docs." %>
<% content_for :canonical_url, "https://internalq.zezlab.com" %>

<div class="kv-page kv-install-page">

  <%# ── Hero ── %>
  <div class="kv-lp-hero">
    <h1 class="kv-lp-headline">Stop answering the same<br>questions again.</h1>

    <p class="kv-lp-sub">
      Upload your company's documents. Your team asks questions in Slack or the web app.
      InternalQ finds the answer — and cites exactly which document it came from.
    </p>

    <p class="kv-lp-example-label">Try it — in any Slack channel:</p>

    <div class="kv-install-example kv-lp-example">
      <span class="kv-mono">@InternalQ</span>
      <span class="kv-lp-example-sep">·</span>
      <span class="kv-mono">What is our parental leave policy?</span>
    </div>

    <p class="kv-lp-trust-line">Answers come only from your uploaded documents — never the open web.</p>

    <div class="kv-lp-cta-row">
      <%= button_to user_google_oauth2_omniauth_authorize_path,
                    method: :post,
                    class: "kv-google-button kv-google-button-lg",
                    form: { data: { turbo: false }, style: "margin: 0;" } do %>
        <span class="kv-google-icon"></span>
        <span>Get started free with Google</span>
      <% end %>

      <div class="kv-lp-cta-meta">
        <span>Free to start · No credit card · 30-second setup</span>
        <span><%= link_to "Already using InternalQ? Log in", new_user_session_path %></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kv-lp-divider"></div>

  <%# ── How it works ── %>
  <div class="kv-lp-section">
    <p class="kv-lp-section-label">How it works</p>
    <div class="kv-lp-steps">
      <div class="kv-lp-step">
        <div class="kv-lp-step-header">
          <span class="kv-lp-step-badge">1</span>
          <span class="kv-lp-step-title">Upload your docs</span>
        </div>
        <p class="kv-lp-step-desc">Add PDFs or Word files — handbooks, onboarding guides, SOPs, policies. Up to 10 MB each. Processed automatically in the background.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="kv-lp-step">
        <div class="kv-lp-step-header">
          <span class="kv-lp-step-badge">2</span>
          <span class="kv-lp-step-title">Connect Slack</span>
        </div>
        <p class="kv-lp-step-desc">One-click OAuth. The bot joins your workspace in under 2 minutes and announces itself so your team knows it's ready.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="kv-lp-step">
        <div class="kv-lp-step-header">
          <span class="kv-lp-step-badge">3</span>
          <span class="kv-lp-step-title">Your team asks</span>
        </div>
        <p class="kv-lp-step-desc">Anyone can @mention the bot in any channel or DM it directly. It replies with the answer and the source document — instantly.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kv-lp-divider"></div>

  <%# ── Why InternalQ ── %>
  <div class="kv-lp-section">
    <p class="kv-lp-section-label">Why teams use InternalQ</p>
    <div class="kv-lp-features">
      <div class="kv-lp-feature">
        <span class="kv-lp-feature-icon">🔒</span>
        <span class="kv-lp-feature-title">Private by design</span>
        <p class="kv-lp-feature-desc">Answers only come from documents you upload. Your content is never mixed with other companies' data or the open web.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="kv-lp-feature">
        <span class="kv-lp-feature-icon">📄</span>
        <span class="kv-lp-feature-title">Sources always cited</span>
        <p class="kv-lp-feature-desc">Every answer points back to the document it came from. Your team knows exactly where the answer came from — no black box.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="kv-lp-feature">
        <span class="kv-lp-feature-icon">🎯</span>
        <span class="kv-lp-feature-title">Honest about gaps</span>
        <p class="kv-lp-feature-desc">If the answer isn't in your docs, InternalQ says so. Admins get a log of unanswered questions — a roadmap for what to document next.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kv-lp-divider"></div>

  <%# ── Use cases ── %>
  <div class="kv-lp-section">
    <p class="kv-lp-section-label">Works great for</p>
    <div class="kv-lp-usecases">
      <span class="kv-lp-usecase-tag">HR &amp; leave policies</span>
      <span class="kv-lp-usecase-tag">Employee handbooks</span>
      <span class="kv-lp-usecase-tag">Onboarding docs</span>
      <span class="kv-lp-usecase-tag">Engineering runbooks</span>
      <span class="kv-lp-usecase-tag">Sales playbooks</span>
      <span class="kv-lp-usecase-tag">SOPs &amp; processes</span>
      <span class="kv-lp-usecase-tag">Benefits guides</span>
      <span class="kv-lp-usecase-tag">IT &amp; security policies</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kv-lp-divider"></div>

  <%# ── Trust bar ── %>
  <div class="kv-lp-trust">
    <div class="kv-lp-trust-item"><span class="kv-lp-trust-dot"></span>Free to get started</div>
    <div class="kv-lp-trust-item"><span class="kv-lp-trust-dot"></span>No credit card required</div>
    <div class="kv-lp-trust-item"><span class="kv-lp-trust-dot"></span>Your documents stay private</div>
    <div class="kv-lp-trust-item"><span class="kv-lp-trust-dot"></span>Listed on the Slack App Directory</div>
  </div>

  <div class="kv-lp-divider"></div>

  <p class="kv-meta-text kv-meta-muted">
    Need help? <%= link_to "Support", support_path %> · <%= link_to "Privacy policy", privacy_path %>
  </p>

</div>
